{
 "format": "protocol-import-v1",
 "source": {
  "kind": "md",
  "filename": "PE_bead_confocal_experiments.md"
 },
 "protocol": {
  "id": "pe-ax-06-sampling-field",
  "title": "PE beads · Exp 06 · Pixels per bead and position in the field",
  "summary": "Image the same beads at 8–40 pixels per bead at equal dose, and the same beads at nine positions in the field, to set sampling and the usable field.",
  "category": "imaging",
  "tags": [
   "pe-beads",
   "confocal",
   "ax-r",
   "characterization",
   "exp-06",
   "sampling",
   "nyquist",
   "field-position",
   "flat-field"
  ],
  "tree": {
   "meta": {},
   "sections": [
    {
     "label": "Overview",
     "children": [
      {
       "kind": "docHeader",
       "body": "Coarse pixels buy field of view; the question is how coarse the integrated metric tolerates.",
       "attrs": {
        "brand": "",
        "title": "Pixels per bead and field position",
        "chips": [
         {
          "text": "Exp 06 of 13"
         },
         {
          "text": "≈2 h"
         },
         {
          "text": "Optics block"
         }
        ]
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "callout",
       "body": "Pins: the scatter of each metric against sampling and sub-pixel position (6a), and what is left of the field-position bias after flat-field correction, i.e. field curvature (6b).",
       "attrs": {
        "type": "note"
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "table",
       "body": "Model prediction (20x, 1 AU; swing over sub-pixel offsets)",
       "attrs": {
        "columns": [
         {
          "key": "ppb",
          "label": "Pixels per bead",
          "align": "left",
          "mono": false
         },
         {
          "key": "px",
          "label": "Pixel",
          "align": "left",
          "mono": false
         },
         {
          "key": "pk",
          "label": "Rim-peak swing",
          "align": "left",
          "mono": false
         },
         {
          "key": "rm",
          "label": "Ring-mean swing",
          "align": "left",
          "mono": false
         },
         {
          "key": "int",
          "label": "Integrated swing",
          "align": "left",
          "mono": false
         }
        ],
        "rows": [
         {
          "ppb": "8",
          "px": "1.00 µm",
          "pk": "28 %",
          "rm": "15 %",
          "int": "4.6 %"
         },
         {
          "ppb": "12",
          "px": "0.67 µm",
          "pk": "39 %",
          "rm": "14 %",
          "int": "1.5 %"
         },
         {
          "ppb": "20",
          "px": "0.40 µm",
          "pk": "14 %",
          "rm": "6.7 %",
          "int": "0.13 %"
         },
         {
          "ppb": "40",
          "px": "0.20 µm",
          "pk": "2.8 %",
          "rm": "2.6 %",
          "int": "<0.01 %"
         }
        ]
       }
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "label": "Materials",
     "children": [
      {
       "kind": "materials",
       "attrs": {
        "rows": [
         {
          "qty": "1",
          "unit": "well",
          "free_text": "Assay beads at high coverage, at a density giving ≥50 isolated beads per 20x field",
          "item_ref": null
         },
         {
          "qty": "1",
          "unit": "ea",
          "free_text": "#1.5 glass-bottom plate",
          "item_ref": null
         }
        ]
       }
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "label": "Settings",
     "children": [
      {
       "kind": "table",
       "body": "Acquisition settings",
       "attrs": {
        "columns": [
         {
          "key": "setting",
          "label": "Setting",
          "align": "left",
          "mono": false
         },
         {
          "key": "value",
          "label": "Value",
          "align": "left",
          "mono": false
         }
        ],
        "rows": [
         {
          "setting": "Mode",
          "value": "Default mode from Exp 05 (repeat in the other leading mode if time allows)"
         },
         {
          "setting": "6a sampling",
          "value": "8, 12, 20, 40 pixels per bead, dwell from the calculator so the dose per µm² is equal"
         },
         {
          "setting": "6b positions",
          "value": "Centre, 4 edge midpoints, 4 corners of the field"
         },
         {
          "setting": "Flat field",
          "value": "From Exp 03, same session"
         }
        ]
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "callout",
       "body": "Before any quantitative acquisition: stand and lasers on for 2–3 h; 561 nm excitation; the same PE emission band (e.g. 570–620 nm) every time; 16-bit with fine integration (the default is 12-bit, so check the file); one HV and one offset for the whole session; background mode at least 50 DN above zero; no saturated pixels. Record the transmitted-light channel with every PE frame: beads are found in it, never in PE. Find focus in transmitted light and hold it with Perfect Focus. Never live-scan PE to focus.",
       "attrs": {
        "type": "critical"
       }
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "label": "Calculator",
     "children": [
      {
       "kind": "calculator",
       "attrs": {
        "label": "Scan geometry and equal-dose dwell",
        "inputs": [
         {
          "name": "m_obj",
          "label": "Objective magnification",
          "widget": "number",
          "unit": "×",
          "default": 20
         },
         {
          "name": "zoom",
          "label": "Scan zoom",
          "widget": "number",
          "unit": "×",
          "default": 1
         },
         {
          "name": "n_px",
          "label": "Frame size",
          "widget": "number",
          "unit": "px",
          "default": 2048
         },
         {
          "name": "bead_d",
          "label": "Bead diameter",
          "widget": "number",
          "unit": "µm",
          "default": 8
         },
         {
          "name": "dwell_ref",
          "label": "Reference dwell",
          "widget": "number",
          "unit": "µs",
          "default": 2
         },
         {
          "name": "ppb_ref",
          "label": "Reference pixels per bead",
          "widget": "number",
          "unit": "px",
          "default": 20
         }
        ],
        "outputs": [
         {
          "name": "field_um",
          "label": "Field side",
          "expr": "17700 / (m_obj * zoom)",
          "unit": "µm",
          "decimals": 0
         },
         {
          "name": "px_um",
          "label": "Pixel size",
          "expr": "field_um / n_px",
          "unit": "µm",
          "decimals": 3
         },
         {
          "name": "ppb",
          "label": "Pixels per bead",
          "expr": "bead_d / px_um",
          "unit": "px",
          "decimals": 1
         },
         {
          "name": "dwell_eq",
          "label": "Dwell for the same dose per µm²",
          "expr": "dwell_ref * (ppb_ref / ppb) ^ 2",
          "unit": "µs",
          "decimals": 2
         },
         {
          "name": "frame_s",
          "label": "Frame time",
          "expr": "n_px ^ 2 * dwell_eq * 1e-6",
          "unit": "s",
          "decimals": 1
         }
        ],
        "table": {
         "dataset": "",
         "columns": []
        }
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "callout",
       "body": "At [!var:ppb] pixels per bead use [!var:dwell_eq] (frame [!var:frame_s]). The AX R offers discrete scan speeds: pick the nearest, record the real dwell, and correct by dose in the analysis.",
       "attrs": {
        "type": "note"
       }
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "label": "Procedure",
     "children": [
      {
       "kind": "heading",
       "body": "Sampling at equal dose",
       "attrs": {
        "code": "6a",
        "rule": true
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "step",
       "body": "Pick one field. Image it at 8, 12, 20 and 40 pixels per bead (zoom about the same centre), each at the equal-dose dwell, in random order."
      },
      {
       "kind": "step",
       "body": "Beads land at random sub-pixel positions, so every phase is sampled without any extra work."
      },
      {
       "kind": "heading",
       "body": "Field position",
       "attrs": {
        "code": "6b",
        "rule": true
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "step",
       "body": "Pick 5 isolated beads. For each, move the stage so the bead sits at the centre, at the 4 edge midpoints and at the 4 corners, imaging each time with the same settings."
      },
      {
       "kind": "step",
       "body": "At each position take a short z-stack (±3 µm, 0.5 µm) as well: the best-focus height against field position gives the field curvature."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "label": "Analysis",
     "children": [
      {
       "kind": "step",
       "body": "6a: for each bead, every metric at each sampling divided by its 40 px value (paired). Report the SD across beads per sampling, which is the sub-pixel scatter."
      },
      {
       "kind": "step",
       "body": "6b: flat-field correct, then plot each metric against distance from the field centre. What remains is field curvature plus any residual shading."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "label": "Decision & record",
     "children": [
      {
       "kind": "callout",
       "body": "Decision: the coarsest sampling that keeps the integrated-metric scatter below 1 % (the throughput lever), and the usable field radius.",
       "attrs": {
        "type": "note"
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "table",
       "body": "Record for every acquisition",
       "attrs": {
        "columns": [
         {
          "key": "field",
          "label": "Field",
          "align": "left",
          "mono": false
         },
         {
          "key": "note",
          "label": "What to write",
          "align": "left",
          "mono": false
         }
        ],
        "rows": [
         {
          "field": "Sampling",
          "note": "Pixels per bead, real dwell"
         },
         {
          "field": "Bead id",
          "note": "Same id across samplings / positions"
         },
         {
          "field": "Position",
          "note": "Field coordinates of the bead"
         }
        ]
       }
      },
      {
       "kind": "callout",
       "body": "Save the .nd2 files as acquired (no 8-bit export, no LUT) in a folder outside the website repo, e.g. BeadConfocalData/<date>_<exp>/, and fill one plate-map CSV row per well or field (columns are listed in Research/PE_bead_confocal_experiments.md, section 7).",
       "attrs": {
        "type": "note"
       }
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 }
}
